# NOTE: this file is normally auto-generated — do not hand-maintain it.
#
# feedmill-backend writes /etc/feedmill/io.conf itself (see
# generateIoConf()/syncIoConf() in src/ethercat.ts) from the configured
# Omron rack and every signal currently mapped to an equipment port —
# never edit it by hand, it'll just get overwritten.
#
# The per-model facts this is generated from — NX_CARD_PRODUCT_ID,
# NX_DI_PDO, NX_DO_PDO, NX_AI_PDO, NX_AO_PDO in src/types.ts — are
# PLACEHOLDERS, unverified. Confirm the real values on the Debian
# target once IgH is installed and the bus is up, and update those
# tables, not this file:
#
#   ethercat slaves -v                  -> vendor_id / product_id per slave
#   ethercat pdos -p <slave position>   -> pdo index:subindex per point
#
# What follows is just a worked example of the format the generator
# produces, for manually testing io_daemon.c before the backend exists
# on the target:
cycle_us 4000
state_path /run/feedmill/io-state.json
command_path /run/feedmill/io-command.txt
slave 2 0x00000083 0x00000000
slave 3 0x00000083 0x00000000
channel I:02.00 2 DI 0x6000 0x01
channel I:02.01 2 DI 0x6000 0x02 count
channel O:03.00 3 DO 0x7000 0x01
channel AI:02.00 2 AI 0x6010 0x01
channel AO:03.00 3 AO 0x7010 0x01
